    <Placemark>
      <name>Hacilar (הצ&apos;ילר (תורכיה))</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Hacilar (הצ&apos;ילר (תורכיה))</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 03. Pottery Neolithic (PN) (-5500 to -4500 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 4: International Comparative Site (&lt; 100m - 1km)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Turkey</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.3.2 (Pages 50)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (03. Pottery Neolithic):</b></p>
<p>Two wells were found. One from layer VI (5750-5600 BCE) is a circular, stone-lined well, 3.2m deep, with a diameter of 1.5m at the top, narrowing to 1.25m at the bottom. The second from layer II (5400-5250 BCE) is a rectangular, stone-lined well located in a courtyard within a fortress. Both had evidence of water drawing mechanisms.</p>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#style_Pottery_Neolithic</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Site_Name"><value>Hacilar</value></Data>
        <Data name="Hebrew_Name"><value>הצ&apos;ילר (תורכיה)</value></Data>
        <Data name="Era"><value>03. Pottery Neolithic (PN) (-5500 to -4500 BCE)</value></Data>
        <Data name="Installation_Type"><value>Deep Well</value></Data>
        <Data name="Region"><value>Turkey</value></Data>
        <Data name="Location_Precision"><value>Tier 4: International Comparative Site (&lt; 100m - 1km)</value></Data>
        <Data name="Dates"><value>-5500 to -4500 BCE</value></Data>
        <Data name="Chapter_Section"><value>2.3.2</value></Data>
        <Data name="Dissertation_Pages"><value>50</value></Data>
        <Data name="Description"><value>Two wells were found. One from layer VI (5750-5600 BCE) is a circular, stone-lined well, 3.2m deep, with a diameter of 1.5m at the top, narrowing to 1.25m at the bottom. The second from layer II (5400-5250 BCE) is a rectangular, stone-lined well located in a courtyard within a fortress. Both had evidence of water drawing mechanisms.</value></Data>
      </ExtendedData>
      <Point>
        <coordinates>30.15,37.6,0</coordinates>
      </Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Kfar Galim North (כפר גלים צפון)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Kfar Galim North (כפר גלים צפון)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 03. Pottery Neolithic (PN) (-5500 to -4500 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Coastal Plain</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.3.1.ב (Pages 49)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (03. Pottery Neolithic):</b></p>
<p>Five circular pits were found, one of which was excavated to 0.7m depth, dug into hard clay and lined with kurkar and limestone. It had an outer diameter of 1.5m and an inner diameter of 0.8-0.9m, identified as a well.</p>]]></description>
