    <Placemark>
      <name>Megadim (מגדים)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Megadim (מגדים)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 03. Pottery Neolithic (PN) (-5500 to -4500 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Coastal Plain</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.3.1.ג (Pages 49)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (03. Pottery Neolithic):</b></p>
<p>Three pits were found, one of which was partially excavated to 0.4m depth. These pits are considered potential wells or water collection points, possibly for capturing fresh water springs.</p>]]></description>
