    <Placemark>
      <name>Tepe Gawra (טפה גאורה)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tepe Gawra (טפה גאורה)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 03. Pottery Neolithic (PN) (-5500 to -4500 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 4: International Comparative Site (&lt; 100m - 1km)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Iraq</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.3.3 (Pages 50)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (03. Pottery Neolithic):</b></p>
<p>A bottle-shaped well, 5m deep, dug into virgin soil at the base of the tel, dating to the Halafian culture (6th millennium BCE). It had an oval opening (1.5x1.2m) and a maximum diameter of 3.1m in the middle, with pottery showing signs of prolonged water exposure.</p>]]></description>
